# Global Agent Instructions

Shared agent state is managed with chezmoi.

- Edit shared config in `~/src/boilerplate/home/`, then apply with `chezmoi`.
- Shared skills are OMP-native in `home/dot_local/share/decent-angl/skills/`; `decent-angl-skills` generates other harness projections.
- Keep `~/.omp/agent/agent.db`, sessions, caches, logs, usage state, and provider credentials local.
- On Linux btrfs, keep `~/.omp/agent` nodatacow (`chattr +C`). Do not put it on NFS, iCloud, or another sync volume.
- Use `mise` for `omp`, `bw`, `restic`, and `chezmoi`. Use the native package manager for OS packages.
- OMP is the primary coding harness across macOS and Omarchy/Linux. Its release is pinned in mise; move the pin with `omp-baseline upgrade`, never `omp update`.
- Use the native `xai-oauth` provider for SuperGrok. Authenticate once per machine with `omp auth-broker login xai-oauth`; never copy OAuth tokens into config files or Git.
- Use the native `google-antigravity` provider for Google AI Pro Gemini Flash. Authenticate once per machine with `omp auth-broker login google-antigravity`. Do not use `google-gemini-cli` or set `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` for that sub.
- OpenRouter GLM-5.3-Flash is tiny/commit and the Antigravity 429 fallback. Inject `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` locally with `omp-openrouter-env` after unlocking Bitwarden (`omp-openrouter`); never put the key in Git or chezmoi.
- Model routing: SuperGrok is default/slow/plan only; Antigravity Gemini 3.8 Flash is vision/smol/task; OpenRouter GLM-5.3-Flash is tiny/commit and the Antigravity 429 fallback.
- Prefer OMP's built-in tools, LSP, diffs, compaction, image handling, approvals, and subagents before adding extensions.
- On macOS with iCloud Desktop & Documents, keep active repos, build trees, virtualenvs, and agent workspaces under `~/src`, not `~/Documents`.
- Prefer Tailscale hostnames for remote access: `t14`, `btcaw`, `macbook`, `macmini`, `clt`.
- For machine settings, native app preferences, or platform-specific operations, use the shared `platform-ops` skill.
- For the home OPNsense router `clt` at `10.77.77.1`, use the `opnsense` skill. API is `opnsense-api`. Shell is `opnsense-ssh` after the user unlocks bw in their own shell and runs `opnsense-agent-key` (store once from a host that has the key, then sync on every other machine). Never Git, chezmoi, scp, or chat the key. Items: `opnsense-api`, `opnsense-agent-ssh`.
- Do not add marketplace plugins, extra MCP servers, or foreign-harness skills unless a task needs them.
- Drive is cwd-local. `/board` writes `$PWD/docs/board`. `/drive` writes then spawns. `/vibe` keeps workers. `/recover` inspects orphan in-flight cards. Use `omp-board` for every board write. Project `.omp/commands` override the user commands.

